{"shortDescription":"Corrected assay results for SH26-27 return 103 g/t AgEq over 17.28 metres, including 416 g/t AgEq over 3.60 metres and 1,192 g/t AgEq over 0.67 metres, marking the re-emergence of high-grade gold mineralization farther south.Correction Notice: Metalsource Mining Inc. is issuing this correction to i…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Corrected assay results for SH26-27 return 103 g/t AgEq over 17.28 metres, including 416 g/t AgEq over 3.60 metres and 1,192 g/t AgEq over 0.67 metres, marking the re-emergence of high-grade gold mineralization farther south."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Correction Notice: Metalsource Mining Inc. is issuing this correction to its news release disseminated on "]},{"type":"b","children":[{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://api.newsfilecorp.com/redirect/JkyNzuYRav","linkText":"November 24, 2026"}}]},{"type":"b","children":[". The Company identified an error in the assay values reported for the broader 17.28-metre composite interval of SH26-27 in Table 1. The corrected grades are substantially higher than previously reported. All other reported assay results remain unchanged. This news release supersedes the original announcement."]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Vancouver, British Columbia--(Newsfile Corp. - November 25, 2026) - ",{"type":"b","children":["Metalsource Mining Inc. ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"CSE:MSM","text":"CSE:MSM"}}," (OTCQB: MSMMF) (FSE: E9Z) (\"Metalsource\" or the \"Company\") "]},"is pleased to provide corrected assay results from its ongoing drill program at Silver Hill, where deep drilling continues to improve management's understanding of the high-grade polymetallic system. SH26-27 returned widespread mineralization over 17.28 metres grading 103 g/t silver equivalent (\"AgEq\"), including 3.60 metres grading 416 g/t AgEq and 0.67 metres grading 1,192 g/t AgEq. SH26-27 demonstrates that mineralization remains open to the south, opening up new target areas for exploration drilling."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Key Highlights"]}]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["High-Grade Gold Mineralization Re-Emerges: "]},"SH26-27 intersected 0.67 metres grading 9.49 g/t gold, 184.86 g/t silver and 20.51% combined lead-zinc, equivalent to 1,192 g/t AgEq, demonstrating the return of high-grade gold mineralization within the southern portion of the system."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["A New Direction for Potential Expansion: "]},"SH26-27 confirms significant polymetallic mineralization farther south of the principal drilling area, beyond an intervening lower-grade zone, opening a compelling new direction for aggressive stepout drilling."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Strengthening the Geological Model: "]},"The contrast between SH26-26 and SH26-27 highlights the variability in grade distribution and provides important geological information for identifying potential controls on higher-grade mineralization and refining future drill targets."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Expanding the Exploration Frontier: "]},"With mineralization visually identified farther south in SH26-45, pending assays and continued aggressive stepout drilling will investigate whether additional mineralized zones extend along strike and at depth, supporting the Company's broader objective of evaluating the ultimate scale of the Silver Hill system."]}]}]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Hole ID"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["From (m)"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["To (m)"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":