"children":["210"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["180"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["-54"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["630"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["Assay Pending"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["SH26-45"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["572089"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["3951715"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["210"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["165"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["-49"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["396"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["Assay Pending"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["SH26-46"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["572089"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["3951715"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["210"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["138"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["-80"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["360"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["Assay Pending"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["SH26-47"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["572089"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["3951715"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["210"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["173"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["-87"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["404"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["Assay Pending"]}]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"i","children":["Table 2: Drill collar locations and layout azimuth/dip for exploration drilling thus far at the Silver Hill Project."]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Metalsource QA/QC protocols are maintained through the insertion of certified reference material (standards), blanks, and duplicates within the sample stream. The drill core is cut in half with a diamond saw, with one half placed in sealed bags and shipped to the laboratory and the other half retained on site. Chain of custody is maintained from the drill to the submittal into the laboratory preparation facility."]},{"type":"p","children":["Analytical testing is performed by ALS Geochemistry (Reno, NV) and ALS Canada (Vancouver, BC). The entire sample is crushed to 70% passing 2mm mesh, with a 250 gram split pulverized to 85% passing minus 75 micron. A four-acid digest is performed on 0.25g of sample to quantitatively dissolve most geological materials. Analysis is performed with a combination of ICP-AES and ICP-MS and fire assay."]},{"type":"p","children":["The exploration results described herein are preliminary in nature and are insufficient to define a mineral resource. Further drilling is required to determine the continuity, geometry, and grade distribution of mineralization. At the time of this release analytical results remain pending."]},{"type":"p","children":["*Metal values used in AgEq calculations are from the 200-day moving average values from 2/6/2026, and all values are in USD. PAu= $124.5/g, PAg= $1.58/g, PCu= $4.9/lb, PPb=$0.90/lbs, PZn=$1.11/lb, 0.00220462262 = grams-to-pounds conversion factor, 22.0462262 = pounds per tonne for 1% metal. Metal recoveries used in the AgEq calculation are Au: 95.5%, Ag: 92.9%, Pb: 89.2%, Zn: 93.8% and Cu 90.8%. These recovery values are derived from batch metallurgical testing used to estimate recoveries of Silver Hill ores, completed in 1988. Individual metal values in the results table are composited values and not factored by recovery. Metal recoveries are applied to their respective component of the AgEq calculation only."]},{"type":"p","children":["https://images.newsfilecorp.com/files/12035/325792_db3fe144e4cecbb8_006full.jpg"]},{"type":"p","children":["To view an enhanced version of this graphic, please visit:"]},{"type":"p","children":["https://images.newsfilecorp.com/files/12035/325792_db3fe144e4cecbb8_006full.jpg"]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Qualified Person"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["All scientific and technical information has been reviewed and approved by Darcy Vis, B.Sc., P.Geo., President of Tripoint Geological Services Ltd., a contractor of the Company, and a Qualified Person as defined under National Instrument (\"NI\") 43-101 - Standards of Disclosure for Mineral Projects."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Silver Hill Project"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Located in the Carolina Terrane, the property is underlain by volcaniclastic and volcano-sedimentary rocks predominantly of Neoproterozoic and Cambrian age. Current interpretations suggest this terrane is an extension of the Avalon Terrane. The property is 1,300 acres located in Davidson County, North Carolina. As the first significant discovery and first silver-producing mine in America, the property is supported by an extensive historic dataset, including drillhole data, underground mapping, historic dumps and underground chip samples. Currently known mineralization extends to 550m from surface, in a steeply trending series of lenses, which remain open in multiple directions."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Byrd-Pilot Mountain Project"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["The Byrd-Pilot Mountain Project is located in central North Carolina within the Carolina Terrane. Initial USGS surveys in the 1980s identified the area as a potential host for a porphyry gold-copper system. Subsequent exploration demonstrated broad gold mineralization in soils, trenches, and shallow RC drilling, coincident with strong self-potential anomalies. Geology shows intense quartz-sericite-pyrite alteration, high-sulfidation signatures, and high-alumina minerals (like Haile and Brewer deposits to the south), suggesting potential for a large epithermal or porphyry-related gold system. Geologic modelling of currently identified mineralization indicates an east-west trend open in multiple directions, with oxidation noted down to a depth of 30m. No drilling has tested the Meridian discovery zone since those 1980s campaigns, leaving potential for significant resource expansion through work commitments of the agreement."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["About Metalsource Mining Inc."]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Metalsource Mining Inc. is a U.S.-focused precious and critical metals exploration company advancing the Silver Hill Project in North Carolina, widely recognized as America's first silver mine. A historically producing mining district dating back to 1839, Silver Hill produced silver, gold, lead and zinc during the formative years of the American mining industry and remains one of the most historically significant mining assets in the United States."]},{"type":"p","children":["The Company is focused on expanding known mineralization, advancing toward a modern resource estimate, and unlocking the broader potential of the Silver Hill district through systematic drilling, geological modeling and modern exploration techniques."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Metalsource Mining"]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"i","children":[{"type":"b","children":["America's First Silver Mine. Modern Exploration. Historic Opportunity."]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["For further information, please contact:"]},{"type":"p","children":["Joe Cullen CEO - Metalsource Mining Inc."]},{"type":"p","children":["Tel: (778) 919-8615"]},{"type":"p","children":["Email: jcullen@metalsourcemining.com"]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Canadian stocks","args":[{"id":"category","value":"stock"},{"id":"market_country","value":"CA"}]},{"title":"TMX Newsfile","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"tmx_newsfile"}]}],"id":"tmx_newsfile:98693fa78094b:0","title":"CORRECTION FROM SOURCE: Metalsource Mining Intercepts Significant Mineralized Zone at Silver Hill, South of Previously Identified High-Grade Mineralization","published":1795613400,"urgency":2,"link":"https://www.newsfilecorp.com/release/325792/CORRECTION-FROM-SOURCE-Metalsource-Mining-Intercepts-Significant-Mineralized-Zone-at-Silver-Hill-South-of-Previously-Identified-HighGrade-Mineralization","relatedSymbols":[{"symbol":"CSE:MSM","logoid":"metalsource-mining","logo":{"style":"single","logoid":"metalsource-mining"}}],"storyPath":"/news/tmx_newsfile:98693fa78094b:0-correction-from-source-metalsource-mining-intercepts-significant-mineralized-zone-at-silver-hill-south-of-previously-identified-high-grade-mineralization/","read_time":518,"provider":{"id":"tmx_newsfile","name":"TMX Newsfile","logo_id":"newsfile","url":"https://www.newsfilecorp.com/"}}